@PSpagnou I hate to argue with @grok but this shows the limitations of LLMs - and it certainly should not be relied on for issues like this (which I do not take lightly).  

CF is defined *with respect to* a particular notion of computation, which for current systems means silicon/digital/algorithmic. Non-computational functionalism indeed includes many other things (continuous dynamics etc).  These can indeed be simulated by digital systems, but simulation is not instantiation unless the simulation target is itself a computation of the equivalent kind.  All this is in my @BBSJournal
 collection, with commentaries and response. https://t.co/6ZFzHrUsUR

